ns_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in 4.4.1.stable\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.1.stable - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated AMD Radeon RX 6750 XT (Advanced Micro Devices, Inc.; 32.0.12033.1030) - AMD Ryzen 5 3600 6-Core Processor (12 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nThe results of the damping coefficient for SoftBody3D nodes while using the Jolt physics engine is wildly different than the results on the Godot Physics engine, and the value is clamped in the engine between 0 and 1 - making the softer flowing that was possible on the older physics engine impossible to replicate.\n\nFor Jolt Physics, even at a damping coefficient maxed out at 1.0 - the resulting simulation is very heavy. Jolt Physics' damping value of 1.0 (max) is roughly equivalent to the old physics' value at 0.01 - meaning we've lost almost all of the control over the stiffness and flow of cloth simulation using the SoftBody3D nodes.\n\nJolt:\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c422b2f3-ca9b-4909-8733-6a5d8f6f588d\n\nGodot:\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e5eaa3af-4268-4407-8ee4-52678ca1ad5a\n\nThere is a difference between 0.01 and 1.0 for the Jolt demonstration, but the tightest setting is still more loose than the loosest setting previously.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nMRP attached. Switch the physics engine between Jolt Physics and Godot Physics and run the test scene to see the stark difference between the soft body simulations. \n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[jolt-softbody-mrp.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/20000088/jolt-softbody-mrp.zip)","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105987/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105987/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}